{"id": "unknown-2026-07-24-005", "date": "2026-07-24", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 30, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["installation_demand", "industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.25, "keywords": ["improve", "loss"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Despite historical failure, cylindrical solar tubes may still find a place in BIPV market, say Japanese scientists", "content": "<p>Solyndra’s cylindrical CIGS solar technology highlighted both the promise and challenges of unconventional PV designs, but a new study from Japan suggests that cylindrical modules may still offer advantages in building-integrated applications.<br />\nResearchers in Japan found that their curved geometry improves cooling, reduces temperature-related losses, and enables more stable energy harvesting under optimized urban installation conditions.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.c", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/07/24/despite-historical-failure-cylindrical-solar-tubes-may-still-find-a-place-in-bipv-market-say-japanese-scientists/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-24-006", "date": "2026-07-24", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 30, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.75, "keywords": ["decline", "weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "China TOPCon cell prices extend decline on weak demand and oversupply", "content": "<p>In a new weekly update for <b>pv magazine</b>, OPIS, a Dow Jones company, provides a quick look at the main price trends in the global PV industry.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/07/24/china-topcon-cell-prices-extend-decline-on-weak-demand-and-oversupply/\">China TOPCon cell prices extend decline on weak demand and oversupply</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/07/24/china-topcon-cell-prices-extend-decline-on-weak-demand-and-oversupply/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "array-2026-07-24-007", "date": "2026-07-24", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 30, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": ["array"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "South African airport tenders 2 MW solar plant", "content": "<p>A tender is open in South Africa for the development of a 2 MW solar array at King Shaka International Airport. The deadline for applications is September 22.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/07/24/south-african-airport-tenders-2-mw-solar-plant/\">South African airport tenders 2 MW solar plant</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/07/24/south-african-airport-tenders-2-mw-solar-plant/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-24-008", "date": "2026-07-24", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 30, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": ["outperform", "loss"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Superhydrophobic nanocomposite coating boosts PV power output by 16%, outperforms manual cleaning", "content": "<p>An Indian research team developed a transparent, nanocomposite coating that makes solar panels superhydrophobic, enabling self-cleaning and reducing dust-related performance losses. Six months of outdoor testing showed coated panels produced 16% more power than dusty panels and 7% more than manually cleaned panels, while also lowering temperature and improving stability.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/07/24/superhydrophobic-nanocomposite-coating-boosts-pv-power-outp", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/07/24/superhydrophobic-nanocomposite-coating-boosts-pv-power-output-by-16-outperforms-manual-cleaning/", "type": "rss"}]}
